From: openSUSE Publishing <publishing@opensuse.org>
Subject: [PATCH] Use open-source EffectCraft tile instead of trademarked ArtCraft mark
Bug: none (downstream trademark removal, not upstreamable)

docs/brand/ (ArtCraft wordmark/mark, LICENSE-brand.txt) is explicitly NOT
open source and must not ship in the tarball, the RPM, or the linked
binary (LICENSE-brand.txt: forks/modified versions must remove the marks).
crates/ui-egui embeds the brand PNG via include_bytes!, so excluding
docs/brand breaks the build. Point that include at the open-source
EffectCraft app tile (assets/app-icon 128 px hicolor PNG, MIT OR
Apache-2.0) instead. The header-bar/About placements stay, only the
artwork changes.

diff --git a/crates/ui-egui/src/header.rs b/crates/ui-egui/src/header.rs
--- a/crates/ui-egui/src/header.rs
+++ b/crates/ui-egui/src/header.rs
@@ -654,11 +654,12 @@
     }
 }
 
-/// The ArtCraft mark as supplied in `docs/brand` (the README's and getartcraft.com's logo; used
-/// unmodified, see `docs/brand/LICENSE-brand.txt`).
-static ARTCRAFT_MARK: &[u8] = include_bytes!("../../../docs/brand/artcraft-mark.png");
+/// Downstream logo (openSUSE): the trademarked ArtCraft marks in docs/brand/
+/// are not shipped; show the open-source EffectCraft app tile instead
+/// (assets/app-icon, MIT OR Apache-2.0, like the repo).
+static ARTCRAFT_MARK: &[u8] = include_bytes!("../../../assets/app-icon/hicolor/128x128/apps/ai.storyteller.effectcraft.png");
 
